  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its design, bulk, mass, scale and siting, would appear incongruous and out of keeping with the prevailing character of the host dwelling, the semi-detached pair, and the wider context of the area. The proposal would overly dominate the rear of the host dwelling, and would present unsympathetic design with regard to the flat roof form. It would thereby cause undue harm to the character and appearance of the area, and would therefore be contrary to the following policies which seek to ensure that developments are sympathetic to local character and historic distinctiveness:National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (December, 2024)The Residential Extensions and Alterations Supplementary Planning Document (February 2012) Policies SP2, DMD1 and DMD5 of The Barking and Dagenham Local Plan (September, 2024)"
